Is this the full extent of your data, these size rows of the data frame?  There is nothing wrong with the formatting of the data, but there are too few data, and likely the units are not correct (because I'm guessing transect lengths are in kilometres and perpendicular distances are in meters?  With only three detections and the nearest being 96 m(?) from the transect, the software fits a horizontal (uniform detection function) to the data, implying that all animals are detected, regardless of distance from the transect.

Plot of fitted detection function as function of perpendicular distance

If detectability is perfect, then size of group cannot influence detectability.

Carry on entering your full data set.  Let us know if the issue persists.

